  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps`: the G205 UNIVERSAL PECKING definition writes `Q208=+99999.999`. It wrote `Q208=FMAX` before. The value is the constant `RETRACT_FEED_MAX`.\r\n- `crates/post/tests/heidenhain_cycles.rs`: the Q parser fails on any Q value that is not a signed number. This covers each cycle that the file tests (G200, G205, G206, G207). The G205 inventory now includes `(208, \"+99999.999\")`, and the test asserts that the program has no `FMAX`.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/heidenhain/drill_peck.nc`: the one word changes.\r\n- `docs/decisions/3102-heidenhain-q208-numeric.md`: the decision record.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- #3102: the iTNC 530 programming station (606425 004 SP20) prefixes the `N100 G205` block with `ERROR =` when it reads `Q208=FMAX`. With `Q208=+60`, the station reads the complete block.\r\n- HEIDENHAIN \"iTNC 530 Cycle Programming\", ID 670388-25 (NC software 60642x-04), cycle 205: Q208 is the feed rate for retraction, input range 0 to 99999.999. The manual lists FMAX, FAUTO and PREDEF as dialogue inputs. Its own NC example writes `Q208=99999`.\r\n- 99999.999 is the top of the range. It asks for the fastest retract that the control permits. `Q208=0` was not chosen: it retracts at the plunge feed Q206, which changes the requested behaviour.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-post` `heidenhain_cycles` `peck_and_deep_have_distinct_documented_native_cycles_and_q_inventory` (and each other test of the file, through the numeric Q check).\r\n- `camcraft-app` `conformance` (the `drill_peck` Heidenhain golden).\r\n\r\n## Gates\r\n\r\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, Windows x86_64): 675 steps, 674 ok. The one red step is `app suites: ai_guide` `ai_guide_calls_match_live_tools_list`. This PR does not cause it: on a CRLF checkout the test finds no \"```json\" fence in `site/content/guide/automate/ai.md`. It is filed as #3119.\r\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`) on the final head 2c9d79af0, Windows x86_64: the change in `crates/post` reaches `app heavy` (197 steps, each target) after one release build. 198 steps ok, 0 failed, 36.5 min. The known-fail steps of #1950 and #2849 are red as expected.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The output was not read on an iTNC 530 station or on a control. The reporter has the station. The physical Fehlmann (NC software 340490-03) check is still open.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Heidenhain DIN/ISO: the G205 peck drilling cycle writes the retraction feed Q208 as a number, so an iTNC 530 reads the block (#3102)\r\n\r\nFixes #3102\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
